# 2. Template Principles

## Purpose

This section establishes the engineering principles that govern the use of the Objective Template.

These principles ensure that every System Objective is documented consistently, supports engineering quality, and remains compatible with the Objective Governance framework.

---

## Template Principles

### TP-01 — Standardized Structure

Every System Objective shall follow the structure defined by this template.

No mandatory section shall be omitted unless explicitly authorized by the applicable governance framework.

---

### TP-02 — Consistency

The same information shall appear in the same location and format across all objective documents to promote readability, maintainability, and engineering consistency.

---

### TP-03 — Completeness

Every mandatory field shall be completed before an objective is submitted for engineering review.

Incomplete objectives shall not progress through the approval process.

---

### TP-04 — Solution Independence

Objective statements shall describe the required engineering outcome and shall not prescribe implementation methods unless governed by a higher-level engineering decision.

---

### TP-05 — Traceability

Every objective shall maintain complete traceability to its governing documents, related objectives, and derived engineering artifacts.

---

### TP-06 — Reusability

The template shall support all approved objective categories without requiring structural modification.

---

### TP-07 — Scalability

The template shall remain suitable for use throughout the growth of the AVIA repository, regardless of the number of objectives managed.

---

### TP-08 — Extensibility

Additional fields or sections may be introduced through approved governance processes without compromising compatibility with previously approved objective documents.

---

### TP-09 — Clarity

Objective documentation shall use precise, unambiguous, and consistent engineering language.

---

### TP-10 — Governance Compliance

Every objective created using this template shall comply with the requirements defined in `OBJECTIVE_GOVERNANCE.md`.
